  "result": "Perfect! The refactoring is complete and fully tested. Here's a summary:\n\n## Refactoring Summary\n\n### What was moved to `src/totals.js`:\n- `lineTotal(line)` - calculates qty \u00d7 unitPrice for a line item\n- `invoiceTotals(invoice)` - calculates subtotal, discount, VAT, voucher, and total for an invoice\n- Dependency: imports `roundCents` from `src/money.js`\n\n### Changes to `src/invoices.js`:\n- Removed function definitions for `lineTotal` and `invoiceTotals`\n- Added: `import { lineTotal, invoiceTotals } from './totals.js';`\n- Added: `export { lineTotal, invoiceTotals };` to maintain backward compatibility\n- Removed unused import of `roundCents` (now only used in totals.js)\n\n### New test file `test/totals.test.js`:\n- 30 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Basic line total calculations\n  - Single and multiple line invoices\n  - Discount calculations (0%, partial, 100%)\n  - Various VAT rates (0%, 9%, 21%)\n  - Voucher handling\n  - Edge cases (empty lines, large amounts, small amounts)\n  - Rounding behavior\n  - Multiple line items with mixed discounts/VAT\n\n### Test Results:\n- **Total tests: 363** (333 original + 30 new)\n- **All tests passing** \u2713\n- **Backward compatibility maintained** \u2713 (existing imports from src/invoices.js still work)\n\nThe refactoring reduces `src/invoices.js` by ~35 lines, improving code organization while keeping the public API unchanged.",
